import java.util.* ;
import java.io.*; 
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class Solution {
    public static ArrayList < Integer > corpFlightBookings(ArrayList < ArrayList < Integer >> bookings, int n) {
        int answer[] =  new int[n];

        for(ArrayList<Integer> booking : bookings){
            int first = booking.get(0);
            int last = booking.get(1);
            int seats = booking.get(2);

            answer[first - 1] += seats;

            if(last < n){
                answer[last] -= seats;
            }
        }

            for(int i = 1; i < n;i++){
                answer[i] += answer[i-1];
            }
        

        ArrayList<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();
        for(int val : answer){
            result.add(val);
        }

        return result;
    }
}

You have been given an array/list “BOOKINGS” of booking details of ‘N’ flights from 1 to ‘N’. Each booking detail contains three positive integers
[first, last, seats] which represent a booking for flights “first” through “last” (inclusive) with “seats” seats reserved for each flight in the range.

Now, you are supposed to return an array/list “ANSWER” of length ‘N’, where answer[i] represents the total number of seats reserved for ith flight.

n = 4;
bookings = {
    {1, 2, 3},
    {2, 3, 2},
    {1, 3, 1},
    {3, 4, 2}
};
[4, 6, 5, 2]

T.C => O(n)
S.C => O(n)
